<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan Mosel 1996 profit down 46 pct.</title>
<headline>Taiwan Mosel 1996 profit down 46 pct.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's Mosel Vitelic Inc said on Tuesday its net profit in 1996 plunged 46 percent to T$4.033 billion from T$7.51 billion in 1995.</p>
<p>Mosel, one of the island's leading dynamic random access memory (DRAM) makers, registered a combined sales revenues of T$10.8 billion in 1996, down from 1995's T$13.65 billion, a company statement said.</p>
<p>It said the company's earnings per share was T$3.1 in 1996.</p>
<p>The figures are unaudited, Mosel said.</p>
<p>The company has attributed the profit and sales slumps to falling DRAM prices since early 1996.</p>
<p>-- Taipei Newsroom(5080815)</p>
</text>
